GAP = 20b leads by ~3.7 points. Claim does not reproduce.

Expected, per the paper, is for the 8B to close and pass once the harness is
instrumented. On this machine the 8B never closes it. Gap is in the same
direction at every seed, so it is not seed noise.

I re-checked the task file, the seed order, and the harness version before
concluding this. All three match the paper.

I then went looking for a cause and I think I found one, but I want to be
careful about how strongly I put it.

note: your 20B baseline looks like a different quant than your 8B.
      The 8B file is q4_k_m. The 20B file behaves more like q4_0 in this
      reproduction — the gap between the two serving paths is larger than it
      should be for a matched pair. I did not fully confirm this by hashing
      the weights, so treat it as a suspicion, not a diagnosis.

Not sure that was intended. If the 20B was served at a worse quant than the
8B, the two cells are not comparable and the crossover number in the paper
is measuring the quant gap rather than the harness effect.

Handing this back rather than filing it. Someone who has the original
weights on hand should check what the 20B cell was actually served from.

